---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Grok Build" description="What Grok Build is: harness for coding and long-running agentic work.">
  <section class="about-content">
    <p class="home-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Features</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Grok Build</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle muted">Harness for coding and sustained agentic workflows.</p>
    <p><strong>Grok Build</strong> is xAI's environment for using Grok models on coding and long-running agent-style tasks. Official messaging treats Build as a harness: where model, tools, and workflow meet for serious engineering work.</p>
    <h2>Grok 4.6 and the Build harness</h2>
    <p>When Grok 4.6 was released, official materials listed Build among the primary surfaces. Elon Musk later stated that Grok 4.6 works best with the Grok Build harness and that the experience is significantly worse without it.</p>
    <h2>What Grok Build is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Coding and engineering workflows that span multiple steps</li>
      <li>Long-running agentic tasks</li>
      <li>Practical evaluation of newer Grok models in the environment xAI recommends</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Build vs Bot vs raw model access</h2>
    <p><a href="/models">Models</a> can be used via API or chat. <a href="/bot">Grok Bot</a> packages teammate-style behaviour. Grok Build is the harness aimed at builders.</p>
    <h2>How Grokati covers Grok Build</h2>
    <p>Announcements that name Build or tie a model release to the harness appear under the Grok Build category.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a href="/features">← All features</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>